{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>That was made at Mount Sinai.</b> Like those that were made in the days of inauguration. Another interpretation — <b>that was made at Mount Sinai</b>: it juxtaposed the daily burnt-offering to the burnt-offering of Mount Sinai — the one that was offered before the giving of Torah — about which it is written (Exodus 24) ״וַיָּשֶׂם בָּאֲגָנֹת״, teaching that it requires a vessel (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:06.901291856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}